{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q19903337","formula":"C₄₄H₇₉NO₅","hill":"C44H79NO5","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":44.0,"H":79.0,"N":1.0,"O":5.0},"names":{"en":"Arachidyl amido cholanoic acid"},"descriptions":{"en":"Aramchol is an investigational drug being developed by Galmed Pharmaceuticals as a first-in-class, potentially treatment for nonalcoholic steatohepatitis,(NASH), a progressive form of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease. It is a conjugate of cholic acid and arachidic acid, and belongs to a class of synthetic fatty-acid/bile-acid conjugates(FABACs), which are composed of endogenous compounds administrated orally, with the aim of good safety and tolerability parameters. Aramchol affects liver fat metabolism and has been shown in a Phase IIa clinical study to significantly reduce liver fat content as well as improve metabolic parameters associated with fatty liver disease."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":18738120,"mass":702.1,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC(=O)N[C@H]1CC[C@]2([C@@H](C1)C[C@H]([C@@H]3[C@@H]2C[C@@H]([C@]4([C@H]3CC[C@@H]4[C@H](C)CCC(=O)O)C)O)O)C","inchikey":"SHKXZIQNFMOPBS-OOMQYRRCSA-N","iupac":"(4R)-4-[(3S,5S,7R,8R,9S,10S,12S,13R,14S,17R)-7,12-dihydroxy-3-(icosanoylamino)-10,13-dimethyl-2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-tetradecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-17-yl]pentanoic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"18738120","atoms":129,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":14.852,"y":4.493,"z":0.272,"el":"C"},{"x":13.922,"y":3.489,"z":-0.392,"el":"C"},{"x":14.469,"y":3.031,"z":-1.742,"el":"C"},{"x":13.515,"y":2.131,"z":-2.536,"el":"C"},{"x":13.208,"y":0.783,"z":-1.872,"el":"C"},{"x":11.875,"y":0.783,"z":-1.118,"el":"C"},{"x":11.62,"y":-0.512,"z":-0.34,"el":"C"},{"x":11.567,"y":-1.794,"z":-1.178,